{"title":"Aczel's Inequality","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p><b>Aczél's Inequality</b> states that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce5c709a67ed2fdb6eac9c049b74c0c5e0074e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1^2&gt;a_2^2+\\cdots +a_n^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"144\" height=\"21\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/e/cfec3b1d2abd2319feeb79744536a05fe6c77402.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_1^2&gt;b_2^2+\\cdots +b_n^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"136\" height=\"19\" />, then\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/e/e4e586c1e0b1d22a10616d6ea1ada94e89009683.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a_1b_1-a_2b_2-\\cdots -a_nb_n)^2\\geq (a_1^2-a_2^2-\\cdots -a_n^2)(b_1^2-b_2^2-\\cdots -b_n^2).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"541\" height=\"19\" /></center>\n<p><br />\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Proof\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Proof</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#General_Form\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">General Form</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Examples\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Examples</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#References\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">References</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Proof\">Proof</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Aczel%27s_Inequality&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Proof\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider the function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/d/0bdcd7b0fef211cf8b56cff554b61bde4769d33d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=(a_1 x - b_1)^2-\\sum_{i=2}^n(a_i x - b_i)^2=$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"295\" height=\"48\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/3/183f777f51eac182b41356157513dfdbb0f542fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a_1^2-a_2^2-\\cdots -a_n^2)x^2-2(a_1b_1-a_2b_2-\\cdots -a_nb_n)x+(b_1^2-b_2^2-\\cdots -b_n^2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"586\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p><p>We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/8/9f8f1b90868fdc824d8006f29a8a59dae0a93103.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f\\left( \\frac{b_1}{a_1} \\right)=-\\sum_{i=2}^n\\left(a_i \\frac{b_1}{a_1} - b_i\\right)^2\\leq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"269\" height=\"50\" />, and from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce5c709a67ed2fdb6eac9c049b74c0c5e0074e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1^2&gt;a_2^2+\\cdots +a_n^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"144\" height=\"21\" /> we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/5/635974403291ec83710de9bb3ed7d3e332088289.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lim_{x\\rightarrow \\infty}f(x)\\rightarrow \\infty$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"118\" height=\"24\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> must have at least one root, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/e/a6ec0db174f3b705df19623976bf4b88ff502f3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Leftrightarrow$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"9\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/0/600033ee366e70b627ec2106c796fa162c123489.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D=(a_1b_1-a_2b_2-\\cdots -a_nb_n)^2- (a_1^2-a_2^2-\\cdots -a_n^2)(b_1^2-b_2^2-\\cdots -b_n^2)\\geq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"608\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"General_Form\">General Form</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Aczel%27s_Inequality&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: General Form\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2><p>\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/6/9f6d44a5c816859f9c159fd1083d4e3566e7911c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_1,\\dots,p_m \\ge1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"112\" height=\"15\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/4/e34b5806283690492db695addf5d65d642873a9c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{i=1}^m\\frac1{p_i} = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"79\" height=\"48\" /> and let </p><center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/9/6197e49bdf70b32797f481c1e4e8e3a0fc36432a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a_{11}, \\dots,a_{1n}),$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"107\" height=\"18\" /></center><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/4/76403adfdd35fb846675aaeaac92daec680a4fba.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\vdots\\]\" width=\"2\" height=\"16\" /></p><center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/6/396e03df5674b31d12ef1d8ced59c780966d25d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a_{m1}, \\dots , a_{mn})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"112\" height=\"18\" /></center> \n<p>be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> sequences of positive real numbers such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/8/a788feea885702ef972fa50d2adedaae1d06fa5c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{i1}^{ p_i} - a_{i2}^{ p_i} - \\dots - a_{in}^{ p_i} &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"191\" height=\"20\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/c/0dca1bf43159be19a8e105dca3ce066612173695.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i=1,\\dots,m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"95\" height=\"16\" />. Then  \n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/0/a70d08ed51a4cb24591f28fb9bf54801251fc6a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\prod_{i=1}^m a_{i1} - \\prod_{i=1}^m a_{i2} -\\dots- \\prod_{i=1}^m a_{in} \\ge\\prod_{i=1}^m  (a_{i1}^{ p_i} - a_{i2}^{ p_i} - \\dots - a_{in}^{ p_i})^\\frac 1{ p_i}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"467\" height=\"53\" /></center>\n<p>with equality if and only if all the sequences are proportional.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Examples\">Examples</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Aczel%27s_Inequality&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Examples\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><b>Olympiad</b>\nSuppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/a/a2a25c2f9720d16d7ab307b6766d3539fad0a05b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1, a_2, \\ldots, a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"103\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/7/9e712ff3c1efcd54de88fdbe99450fed2d84ad55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_1, b_2, \\ldots, b_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"95\" height=\"16\" /> are real numbers such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/0/770529fbbcc61607410c324516d3fcfed3445add.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(a_1 ^ 2 + a_2 ^ 2 + \\cdots + a_n ^ 2 -1)(b_1 ^ 2 + b_2 ^ 2 + \\cdots + b_n ^ 2 - 1) &gt; (a_1 b_1 + a_2 b_2 + \\cdots + a_n b_n - 1)^2.\\]\" width=\"537\" height=\"19\" /> Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/3/9f39ddc3e9822221804dc513640b24e02e4b1d8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1 ^ 2 + a_2 ^ 2 + \\cdots + a_n ^ 2 &gt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"173\" height=\"19\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54db4c6a7093f088cc8fe60dc3d878374edf001e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_1 ^ 2 + b_2 ^ 2 + \\cdots + b_n ^ 2 &gt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"167\" height=\"19\" />. (USA TST 2004)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"References\">References</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Aczel%27s_Inequality&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: References\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li>Mascioni, Vania, <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.maths.soton.ac.uk/EMIS/journals/JIPAM/v3n5/045_02_www.pdf\">A note on Aczél-type inequalities</a>, JIPAM volume 3 (2002), issue 5, article 69.</li>\n<li>Popoviciu, T., Sur quelques inégalités, Gaz. Mat. Fiz. Ser. A, 11 (64) (1959) 451–461</li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Aczel%27s_Inequality&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Inequalities\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Inequalities\">Inequalities</a></li></ul>\n<p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Aczel%27s_Inequality&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\n